vibePDA C port - VT102 and FreeDOS console
==========================================

Build targets (GNU-style Makefile):

  make                  Native Linux (x86_64 or i386)
  make TARGET=linux-ia32  Force 32-bit Linux (requires gcc -m32)
  make TARGET=dos         FreeDOS (requires DJGPP: i586-pc-msdosdjgpp-gcc)

Install:

  make install [PREFIX=/usr/local] [DESTDIR=/staging]

Terminal and console:

  - VT102: Use a VT100/VT102 compatible terminal or emulator (80x24).
  - DOS:   Standard 80x25 console. Build with TARGET=dos (DJGPP).

Architectures:

  - Linux x86_64: default when building on 64-bit host.
  - Linux i386:   make TARGET=linux-ia32 (requires gcc-multilib / libc6-dev-i386 on Debian).
  - FreeDOS:      make TARGET=dos (32-bit DPMI via DJGPP cross-compiler).

GNU standards:

  make all       Build
  make clean     Remove built files
  make install   Install to $(DESTDIR)$(prefix)
  make dist      Create tarball
